## 🎉 Rotating Card – Hover‑to‑Rotate Demo

Below is a minimal, self‑contained example that shows a “card” (a rectangular block) that rotates around its Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy‑paste the code into an `.html` file and open it in your browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣ Basic reset & layout ---------- */
body {
  display:flex;
  justify-content:center;
  align-items:center;
  min-height:100vh;
  margin:0;
  background:#f0f0f0;
  font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣ Card container ---------- */
.card {
  width:260px;
  height:360px;
  perspective:800px;          /* gives depth to the 3D effect */
  cursor:pointer;
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣ Card inner (the part that actually rotates) ---------- */
.card__inner {
  width:100%;
  height:100%;
  position:relative;
  transition:transform 0.6s ease;   /* smooth animation */
  transform-style:preserve-3d;      /* keep children in 3D space */
}

/* ---------- 4️⃣ Front & Back faces ---------- */
.card__face {
  position:absolute;
  width:100%;
  height:100%;
  backface-visibility:hidden;       /* hide backside when flipped */
  border-radius:12px;
  overflow:hidden;
  box-shadow:0 4px 12px rgba(0,0,0,.15);
}

.card__face--front {
  background:#fff;
  display:flex;
  flex-direction:column;
  justify-content:center;
  align-items:center;
  padding:20px;
  text-align:center;
}

.card__face--back {
  background:#4a90e2;
  color:#fff;
  transform:rotateY(180deg);        /* place it behind the front */
  display:flex;
  justify-content:center;
  align-items:center;
  padding:20px;
  text-align:center;
}

/* ---------- 5️⃣ Hover effect ---------- */
.card:hover .card__inner {
  transform:rotateY(180deg);         /* flip the card */
}
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card">
  <div class="card__inner">
    <!-- Front face -->
    <div class="card__face card__face--front">
      <h2>Front Side</h2>
      <p>Hover over this card to see the magic!</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Back face -->
    <div class="card__face card__face--back">
      <h2>Back Side</h2>
      <p>Here’s some hidden content.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens | Why |
|------|--------------|-----|
| **1** | `perspective` on `.card` | Gives depth so the rotation looks 3‑D. |
| **2** | `.card__inner` has `transform-style: preserve-3d` | Keeps child elements in 3‑D space. |
| **3** | `backface-visibility: hidden` on faces | Hides the backside when it’s turned away. |
| **4** | `transform: rotateY(180deg)` on back face | Places the back face behind the front. |
| **5** | On hover, `.card__inner` rotates 180° | Flips the card to reveal the back. |

### Tweaks & Extensions

| Want to change? | How to do it |
|-----------------|--------------|
| **Rotate around X‑axis** | Replace `rotateY(180deg)` with `rotateX(180deg)` in both the back face and hover rule. |
| **Add more content** | Add more elements inside `.card__face--front` or `.card__face--back`. |
| **Different speed** | Change `transition:transform 0.6s ease` to a shorter or longer duration. |
| **Add shadow on hover** | Add `box-shadow` to `.card:hover .card__inner`. |
| **Use CSS variables** | Define `--card-width`, `--card-height`, etc., for easier theming. |

Enjoy experimenting! 🚀
